# Native Face Pipeline

## Bundle layout

- `src/bin/face_pipeline` — executable
- `src/bin/lib/*.dylib` — macOS runtime libs (`@executable_path/lib`)
- `src/bin/models/` — ONNX models (SCRFD, RF-DETR, optional OSNet)

## Build flow (macOS)

1. `yarn build:native` — CMake + compile (`-DFACE_PIPELINE_ENABLE_GMC=OFF` by default)
2. `yarn stage:native:mac` — install to `src/bin`, run `scripts/stage-native-macos.sh` (collect dylibs -> `lib/`, rewrite install names, ad-hoc sign)
3. `yarn build` — CEP-only build; precheck validates native bundle
4. `yarn zxp` — runs `verify:native` first, then packages

## Key scripts

- `scripts/stage-native-macos.sh <exe> <out_dir>` — bundles dylibs into `out_dir/lib`, relinks to `@executable_path/lib/`, codesigns
- `scripts/verify-native-bundle.mjs` — checks `src/bin` structure
- `scripts/setup_onnx_models.sh` — fetches/copies ONNX models into `src/bin/models`

## GMC

- Default: translation-only fallback (no OpenCV)
- OpenCV GMC: `-DFACE_PIPELINE_ENABLE_GMC=ON` in CMake, `brew install opencv` — adds many dylibs

## Runtime

- CEP/Node spawns `face_pipeline`, passes frame paths via stdin
- `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` includes `bin` and `bin/lib` on macOS
